course: dictionary
lesson: 14152
title: Soft words that hide the truth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are chosen to make something sound less bad than it is. To misremember means to remember something wrongly, like mixing up a date. Grown-ups in charge sometimes use it in a different way.
explain: «The minister said he had never met the boss, but photos showed them shaking hands. Later he said he had simply misremembered.» Here misremembered does not just mean got a memory wrong. It is a softer way of saying he said something untrue, and it avoids the harsher word lied.
explain: Ask yourself: is this a real mix-up, or a way to avoid blame? Look at the words around it. Did the person get caught saying something false? Then the word is probably a polite cover story, not an honest slip of memory.
fact: Misremember means to remember something wrongly.
fact: «I misremembered the date of the test, so I arrived a day late.» This is the simple meaning: a real mix-up in memory.
fact: A euphemism is a softer, politer word used in place of a harsher one.
fact: «Misremembered» can be a euphemism: an official may use it to mean said something untrue, without saying «lied».
fact: Official words can be used as spin, to make a fault sound like an honest mistake. Check the facts before you believe an excuse.
exercise: «I misremembered my friend's address, so I went to the wrong house.» What does misremembered mean here? | I forgot my own name | *I remembered it wrongly by mistake | I wrote the address in gold ink | I told a lie on purpose to hide something
exercise: After a video proved he had said something false, a politician said, «I misremembered.» What does this suggest? | He is describing a film he saw | He was asleep during the video | *He said something untrue and used a softer word to cover it | He remembered everything perfectly
exercise: Why might an official choose misremembered instead of lied? | *It sounds softer and avoids blame | It means happy | It is a longer, harder word | It means exactly the same as lied, so there is no reason to change it
test: «Nadia misremembered where she put her bag.» What does misremembered mean? | Gave the bag to her brother | *Remembered wrongly by mistake | Threw the bag away | Found the bag under the bed
test: What is a euphemism? | *A softer, politer word used in place of a harsher one | A word from another country | A very long word | A word that means happy
exam: The politician said he had misremembered after the truth came out. What is the spin in this word? | *He is using a softer word to hide an untruth | He is describing a film he saw | He is confessing and asking for help | He has the best memory in the country
